course: dictionary
lesson: 7756
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and pupil is one of them. To choose the right meaning, read the words around it. Those words are its context, and they leave clues.
explain: A pupil is a child who goes to school and learns from a teacher. «Well known to staff» is a joking UK way to say the pupil is often in trouble, so here pupil means a child at school.
explain: Pupil can also mean anyone who learns from a teacher, like a piano pupil. The third meaning is different: the pupil of the eye is the black circle in the middle that lets light in. Look for clues such as eye, light or squint.
explain: Swap your meaning into the sentence to check it. In «Walk out of a dark cinema into bright sunshine and you squint: the black dot in your eye, the pupil, shrinks fast», only the eye meaning fits, because the black dot in your eye is what shrinks.
fact: Pupil is a noun. Its plural is pupils.
fact: A pupil is a child who goes to school and learns from a teacher.
fact: In the UK, Ireland, Australia and New Zealand, pupil is common; Americans usually say student.
fact: The pupil of the eye is the black circle in the middle that lets light in. It gets smaller in bright light and bigger in the dark.
fact: In maths, pupils are counted, and they can be shared into groups or rows. «Each pupil» can mark a rate.
exercise: «Well known to staff» is a joking UK way to say the pupil is often in trouble. What does pupil mean here? | *A child who goes to school | The black circle in the eye | A piano player | A teacher who gives lessons
exercise: Walk out of a dark cinema into bright sunshine and you squint: the black dot in your eye, the pupil, shrinks fast. What does pupil mean? | The coloured ring around the eye | *The black circle in the middle of the eye that lets light in | Child at school | Piano learner
exercise: Americans usually say «student». Which country is more likely to say «pupil»? | *Australia | Brazil | Egypt | Japan
test: Fire-bellied toads have pupils shaped like a triangle or a heart. What does pupils mean in this sentence? | Groups of toads sold in shops | Lessons given by a teacher | *The black circle in the middle of the eye | Children learning in a school
test: Mia's piano pupil plays every Tuesday. What does pupil mean in this sentence? | *Someone who learns from a teacher, like a piano pupil | A child who goes to school | The black circle in the middle of the eye | A toad with spots
exam: Which sentence uses pupil to mean the black circle in the eye? | «Each pupil in the class got a book.» | «Our pupil learned to play the violin.» | «The pupil raised her hand to answer the question.» | *«The pupil shrank fast in the bright sunshine.»
